    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="0925" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg843"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Canisius to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 8, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:* * * * The news received here per telegraph
                    that you have demanded of Austria the discontinuation of sending any more
                    volunteers to Maximilian, of Mexico, has created here quite a sensation. The
                    people of Austria feel now, in their distress, more than ever, that this
                    enterprise of Maximilian, and the subsequent agreement made by this government
                    to aid him by sending soldiers to that distant country, of no value to the
                    people of this empire, was a great mistake.</p>
                <p>I found in this morning’s paper the following item:</p>



                <xi:include href="d755-a1.xml" xpointer="d755-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
